    "letter":  {
                   "date":  "August 29, 2026 · Our 25th Anniversary",
                   "title":  "Twenty-Five Years, Still You",
                   "greeting":  "Bodin, my Baby,",
                   "paragraphs":  [
                                      "Twenty-five years. That number sounds very serious. We, however, are still not very serious people.",
                                      "On August 29, 2001, neither of us knew exactly what we were beginning. You poked my ass, I was embarrassed, you did not care, and somehow you started the best trouble of my life.",
                                      "Now look at us. A quarter of a century later, we are older, grayer, wiser in a few places, and still capable of arguing about something so small that neither of us remembers how it started.",
                                      "People call twenty-five years the silver anniversary. Silver sounds elegant and peaceful. After everything we have survived—and everything we have put each other through—I think ours should be made of titanium.",
                                      "We have lived through the exciting days, the difficult days, the tired days, and all those ordinary days nobody takes pictures of. Those ordinary days matter to me more than I knew they would.",
                                      "Because that is where our life really happened.",
                                      "It happened in the routines. In the teasing. In the pouting lips. In the checking on each other. In making a home. In being apart and finding our way back. In laughing five minutes after we both swore we were still annoyed.",
                                      "I used to think love was mostly about the big moments. After twenty-five years, I know better.",
                                      "Love is showing up when it would be easier to stay quiet. Love is learning the same person again as both of you change. Love is knowing exactly how to get on each other's nerves—and also knowing exactly how to make things right.",
                                      "You still demand attention. You still expect to be babied. You still give me that look when I have failed one of your inspections. And yes, sometimes you still drive me completely crazy.",
                                      "But you are my favorite kind of crazy.",
                                      "I love the woman you were when we met, but I am even more in love with the woman you are now. Stronger. More certain. More beautiful. Still stubborn. Still gorgeous. Still able to make me wonder how this hot, sexy woman kept choosing me.",
                                      "I have watched you protect our family, carry more than people realize, and keep going even when life asked too much from you. I hope you know how deeply I admire you.",
                                      "You did not just share twenty-five years with me. You helped shape the man I became.",
                                      "You challenged me when I needed it. You believed in me when I did not say I needed it. You made our home feel like home because you were in it.",
                                      "Twenty-five years does not mean we were perfect. It means we kept coming back, kept reaching for each other, and kept choosing us.",
                                      "That is what I am proud of.",
                                      "I am proud of the laughter. I am proud of the scars. I am proud of every version of us that refused to give up on the next one.",
                                      "If I could go back to the beginning, knowing every argument, every hard season, every ridiculous misunderstanding, and every blanket-stealing battle ahead of us, I would still walk straight toward you.",
                                      "I might protect my ass this time, but I would still choose you.",
                                      "And I will keep choosing you—not only because of everything we have already lived, but because I still want everything that comes next.",
                                      "I want more ordinary mornings. More corny jokes. More trips. More projects you supervise while I pretend I am in charge. More gray hair. More memories. More years of you being my baby.",
                                      "I cannot promise that I will suddenly become mature after twenty-five years. At this point, we should both accept that the evidence is against me.",
                                      "But I can promise to show up. To reach for your hand. To take care of you. To make you laugh. To annoy you with commitment and consistency. And to love you on purpose.",
                                      "Bodin, you are still the person I want beside me when life is wonderful, when life is hard, and when absolutely nothing special is happening.",
                                      "We made it to twenty-five years, Baby. Still laughing. Still fighting for each other. Still us.",
                                      "Happy 25th anniversary to the woman who started all this trouble—and made every year worth it.",
                                      "I love you, Bodin. Then, now, and in every year still waiting for us."
                                  ],
                   "closing":  "Always yours,",
                   "signature":  "Papi"
               }
}
